# impeccable design-tool cache (regenerated locally)
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
.impeccable/live/

# Credentials. The repo is public, so these are ignored before they exist —
# `.dev.vars` is where wrangler expects local secrets and it is one `touch`
# away from being committed by anyone working here.
google-search-console-api.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Internal planning docs — kept locally, not published to the remote.
# Rooted so it never matches the app's product docs (apps/web/src/content/docs).
/docs/

# The project reading (`pulse`) and everything it writes. A reading names what
# the tool failed at and how few people used it, so unlike its two committed
# siblings in scripts/ it stays on this machine. Output lands in /docs/reviews/,
# already covered above.
/.claude/skills/pulse/

# The `opportunity` lens, which is the same reading asked one question at a
# time. It runs pulse's own --segments mode and its text quotes the readings
# that mode produced, so publishing it would leak exactly what /docs/ hides.
/.claude/skills/opportunity/

# The napkin, for the same reason. It was tracked, and notes written while
# reading the counters quoted the reading straight into a public file — Run
# counts, per-extension Visit/day figures, a pointer to /docs/reviews/. Keeping
# /docs/ private only works if nothing else repeats what it says. History still
# holds the old entries; this stops the next one.
/.claude/napkin.md

# Redesign working files — kept locally, not published to the remote.
/redesign/
.mcp.json

# Real-document fixtures for extraction-quality measurement. These are files
# real software wrote (Word, Excel, a LaTeX engine) or a generator produced, and
# they may be somebody's actual documents. The committed suite deliberately uses
# hand-built bytes instead (see fixtures/pdf.ts) so a reader can see what makes
# each one interesting; this directory is measurement input, not test data.
# The generator script is tracked, its output is not.
/packages/core/tests/fixtures/real/*
!/packages/core/tests/fixtures/real/README.md
!/packages/core/tests/fixtures/real/generate.mjs

# Tesseract language models. Running OCR under node caches the model into the
# working directory — 5.2 MB per language, downloaded from a CDN — so any OCR
# run leaves one behind wherever it was started from. Nothing here should ever
# be committed; the same files belong on our own origin (see the OCR options on
# extractOfficeDocument), not in git.
*.traineddata
*.traineddata.gz
